{
  title = "an applied sighting joins its static twin whatever its co-members are";
  adr = "0034, 0016, den-hoag-c4ucc";
  what = "`aspect-applied-sighting-joins-its-static-twin`: on ADR-0016 r4's excluded float domain one factory makes an int the mint takes and an `==` float it refuses; the static `twine` holds both, so they are one class. `hitch`'s applied int joins that class through the int member's digest, whatever the float member is, so `mooring` receives one `cord` id; `bend`'s applied float, which the mint refuses, is keyed within its own instance (P2-b). Before (the class-regime gate), the applied int was keyed by its content digest beside the static class.";
}
